---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="BullDozer privacy policy — no accounts, no tracking, no personal data collected.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
      <h1>BullDozer — Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="sub">Last updated: 27 September 2026</p>

      <p>BullDozer is a free app and website that turns public statistics into
      charts, country profiles, maps and a data quiz. It is designed to work
      without accounts and without collecting personal data.</p>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Data we collect</h3>
        <p>The app does not ask for a name, email, phone number or login. We do
        not use analytics, advertising or third-party trackers inside the app.
        The one thing that leaves your device is a question you choose to ask in
        Ask AI — see below.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Ask AI</h3>
        <p>When you pick a country in Ask AI, or type a question there, the
        country and the question are sent to our server at bot.azenha.ai to
        produce an answer. The server passes them, with that country's published
        figures, to an AI provider — Anthropic (Claude) or Cloudflare Workers
        AI — only to write the answer, under that provider's API terms. We do
        not store your questions or the answers. Your IP address is used for a
        per-minute limit on questions and is not kept. Nothing is sent unless you
        open Ask AI and choose a country.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Data stored on your device</h3>
        <p>Your favourites, quiz progress and theme preference are saved locally
        on your device only. Public datasets are cached locally so the app works
        offline. This information never leaves your phone and is removed when you
        uninstall the app.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Network</h3>
        <p>The app downloads public data files from
        <a href={`${base}/`}>azenha.ai/bulldozer</a>. These are simple file
        requests and include no personal information. Opening a source or story
        link launches your browser and is subject to that site’s own policy.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Telegram bot</h3>
        <p>If you press Watch in our Telegram bot, it stores your Telegram chat
        id and the country or figure you chose, so it can message you when they
        change — nothing else about you. Stop watching deletes it.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Notifications</h3>
        <p>Any reminders are scheduled as local notifications on your device. No
        notification data is sent to a server.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Children</h3>
        <p>The app is suitable for all ages. It does not ask for or store
        personal data from anyone.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Changes</h3>
        <p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this
        page.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Contact</h3>
        <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:agent@azenha.ai">agent@azenha.ai</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
